This is a limiting finding, not fabricated output.

## What WAS executed (documented FALLBACK, not pydeseq2/DESeq2)
`ube2m_kegg_gsea.py` implements a DESeq2-equivalent NB GLM (median-of-ratios size
factors with offsets, MoM dispersion + parametric trend + prior blend, per-gene NB
MLE via L-BFGS-B with exact gradient, Wald test, BH padj, legacy normal-prior
lfcShrink) and applies the brief's filters in order. Results are TENATIVE:
- funnel: 21,884 -> baseMean>10: 11,676 -> +p<0.05: 5,773 -> +|log2FC raw|>1: 2,184
  (865 up / 1,319 down in KD vs CTRL).
- Sensitivity (filter on shrunken lfc): 1,254 DEG (secondary).
- p-value inflation: 49% of expressed genes have p<0.05; label-permutation check
  (`diagnostic_permutation_check.py`) shows the null is inflated (mean ~24%):
  PC1 (48.3%) aligns with KL-vs-WL but PC2 (38.7%) isolates replicate 3 of BOTH
  groups (KL3/WL3) — a dominant sample-level axis with n=3 vs n=3 makes Wald p-values
  anti-conservative regardless of dispersion shrinkage. DEG counts are therefore
  likely overestimates pending real DESeq2 (or a batch-adjusted design, out of brief scope).
- Group assumption (KL=KD, WL=CTRL, name-based): Ube2m expression per group NOT
  verifiable offline (no mapping). Proxy support: PC1 separates KL1-3 from WL1-3.

